This image contains FRRouting 10.7.1 from upstream commit
f8c0b08dcb0c78f9e42b9b86ae70b049e4e617c1, with Weblab vtysh extensions.
The source archive and applied patch are included in this directory.
FRR's source retains its individual copyright and license notices, including
COPYING and doc/licenses/LGPL-2.1. The FRR patch is GPL-2.0-or-later, like vtysh.
The Weblab LLDP/SNMP/VLAN/VRRP backends and build tooling are MIT, like Weblab.
lldpd and Alpine packages retain their upstream licenses; see their installed
package metadata. lldpd source: https://github.com/lldpd/lldpd/tree/1.0.19
This is a Weblab extension image, not an unmodified upstream FRRouting release.
The image also includes Alpine's Net-SNMP packages. Their individual upstream
copyright/license notices remain applicable; see installed package metadata and
https://www.net-snmp.org/about/license.html. SNMP service integration is Weblab
code under MIT. FRR routing-protocol SNMP modules are not enabled by this recipe.
Routed VLAN backend integration is Weblab code under MIT. It uses Linux
802.1Q interfaces; it does not modify the kernel or add an upstream FRR feature.
IPv4 VRRP interface provisioning is Weblab code under MIT. FRR still implements
the election protocol and Master/Backup state transitions.

Weblab modifications dated 2026-10-15. Corresponding source and build recipes
accompany published binaries; see SOURCES.md and packages.json. Package metadata
for inherited FRR APKs describes the base, not the rebuilt Weblab executables.
